### Agent Switching Handoff

If switching agents mid-task, the new agent should:

1. **Read `.cursor/state/current-position.md`** — Understand exactly where the previous agent left off
2. **Read open PR description** (if exists) — Understand intent and acceptance criteria
3. **Run tests** — Verify current state is green
4. **Ask clarifying questions** — If state is ambiguous

### Memory Artifacts (Persistent Across Sessions)

- **`.cursor/state/current-position.md`** — Always current (updated after every action)
- **`.cursor/state/workstream-progress.json`** — Machine-readable progress tracking
- **`.cursor/state/session-notes/YYYY-MM-DD-HH-MM.md`** — Per-session detailed notes
- **Git commit history** — Granular action log
- **PR descriptions** — Intent and acceptance criteria
- **Test coverage** — Living documentation of behavior

### Automatic Context Sharing

To enable seamless agent switching:

1. **State file is source of truth** — No tribal knowledge
2. **Tests document behavior** — No "trust me, it works"
3. **Flags gate all new surfaces** — No invisible dependencies
4. **Owned paths prevent conflicts** — No merge hell
5. **CI validates correctness** — No broken state

### Context Preservation Checklist

Before ending ANY session:
- [ ] `.cursor/state/current-position.md` updated
- [ ] All changes committed with clear messages
- [ ] Tests pass locally (`ruff check`, `mypy`, `pytest`, `npm test`, `npm run build`)
- [ ] Pushed to origin (if on feature branch)
- [ ] PR opened (if slice complete)
- [ ] Next steps documented in state file

### Figma Design Vision (UI Truth)

From master plan + Figma Make prototype:
- **Command Center aesthetic**: Terminal-style input, world map, draggable panels
- **Core verbs**: Examine, Monitor, Pin, Share, Export
- **Layout**: Top 60% = map + layers, Bottom 40% = draggable modules
- **Trust UI**: Citations, confidence, dissent, provenance always visible
- **Keyboard-first**: Omnibox/terminal always reachable
- **Progressive disclosure**: Short high-signal by default, expand on request

**Figma URL**: https://www.figma.com/make/yGEihhyU0cCiVNi3DILbAt/Landing-Page-for-WatchfulEye

### Non-Negotiables (Never Forget)

1. **Sacred surfaces** (never break):
   - Main News Feed
   - Custom News Feed
   - Telegram Intel Reports
   - Intel Reports
   - AI Analysis Modal

2. **Flag discipline**:
   - All V3 features behind `V3_*` flags
   - Default OFF in production
   - Rollback = flip flag OFF

3. **File ownership**:
   - Each workstream owns its paths
   - Hot files require justification
   - WS0 owns contracts/schemas

4. **CI discipline**:
   - Green required for merge
   - CodeRabbit review addressed
   - One workstream slice per PR

5. **Production isolation**:
   - NEVER deploy V3 to prod until ready
   - Prod is frozen
   - Staging only via master-only worktree

